erde_json = \"1.0\"\nclipboard = \"0.5\"                                       # cross\u2011platform clipboard\nrodio = \"0.17\"                                          # audio playback\nanyhow = \"1.0\"                                          # error handling\ndotenvy = \"0.15\"                                        # load .env files (optional)\n```\n\n> **Why these crates?**  \n> * `tokio` \u2013 async runtime needed by `reqwest`.  \n> * `reqwest` \u2013 HTTP client with streaming support.  \n> * `serde`/`serde_json` \u2013 parse JSON responses.  \n> * `clipboard` \u2013 read the system clipboard.  \n> * `rodio` \u2013 play back the audio bytes.  \n> * `anyhow` \u2013 simple error handling.  \n> * `dotenvy` \u2013 optional, lets you keep your API key in a `.env` file.\n\n---\n\n## 3. `src/main.rs`\n\n```rust\nuse anyhow::{anyhow, Context, Result};\nuse clipboard::ClipboardProvider;\nuse dotenvy::dotenv;\nuse rodio::{Decoder, OutputStream, Sink};\nuse reqwest::Client;\nuse serde::Deserialize", "Sure thing! To make the \u201cFilters\u201d section clearer, I\u2019ll need the current version of the document (or at least the part that contains the Filters). Once I have that, I can rewrite it in a more readable format and label", "", "", "", "", ""], "errors": ["", "", "", "", "", "", "", ""], "max_output_tokens_per_s": 38.0, "max_concurrent_requests": 3, "rtfx": 0.0, "spec_decode_acceptance_rate": 29.020044543429847, "spec_decode_acceptance_length": 2.451002227171492, "spec_decode_num_drafts": 898, "spec_decode_draft_tokens": 4490, "spec_decode_accepted_tokens": 1303, "spec_decode_per_position_acceptance_rates": [0.6681514476614699, 0.3730512249443207, 0.20935412026726058, 0.13140311804008908, 0.06904231625835189], "mean_ttft_ms": 121.16855900967494, "median_ttft_ms": 111.36270448332652, "std_ttft_ms": 19.734666243726114, "p50_ttft_ms": 111.36270448332652, "p90_ttft_ms": 148.4850017237477, "p99_ttft_ms": 153.15398773760535, "mean_tpot_ms": 10.350211506581887, "media